          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "to keep this naming convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 63.75,
          "en": "of being descriptive about what's in a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.75,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "Now, this newly created TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "should simply hold a class, which I export, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 72,
          "en": "which will name \"shortenPipe.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.937,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "Now this shortenPipe, this class needs to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "one special method to be usable as a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "And while it's not strictly necessary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 86.4,
          "en": "it's a good practice to implement a certain interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 89.43,
          "en": "which requires you to implement that method.",
